# COMPLETE EXPLANATION OF MERN BLOG DEPLOYMENT ON AWS

This assignment deploys a MERN Stack blog application on AWS using:

| Technology    | Purpose                 |
| ------------- | ----------------------- |
| MongoDB Atlas | Database                |
| Express.js    | Backend framework       |
| React + Vite  | Frontend                |
| Node.js       | JavaScript runtime      |
| Nginx         | Web server              |
| PM2           | Backend process manager |
| EC2           | Cloud virtual machine   |

---

# COMPLETE ARCHITECTURE

```text id="xy2kgx"
User Browser
      ↓
Frontend EC2 (Nginx + React)
      ↓ API Calls
Backend EC2 (Node + Express)
      ↓
MongoDB Atlas Cloud Database
```

---

# WHY TWO EC2 INSTANCES?

| Instance     | Work                  |
| ------------ | --------------------- |
| Frontend EC2 | Hosts React website   |
| Backend EC2  | Runs Node/Express API |

---

# WHY SEPARATE SERVERS?

Advantages:

✅ Better scalability

✅ Better security

✅ Easier maintenance

✅ Professional deployment architecture

