# FRONTEND `.env`

```env id="jhmpt4"
VITE_API_URL=http://BACKEND_IP:5000/api
```

---

# WHY IMPORTANT?

Frontend must know backend API location.

---

# WHY `/api`?

Because backend routes start with:

```javascript id="v0b0jl"
app.use("/api", routes)
```

---

# WHY REBUILD AFTER `.env` CHANGE?

Vite embeds environment variables during build time.

So after changing `.env`:

```bash id="n1o2m7"
npm run build
```

is mandatory.

